+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at the trades that closed within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), for a pair (ordered by close time). If the most recent `trade_limit` (or more) trades in a row all resulted in a loss, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+A single winning (or break-even) trade resets the streak, so the count always reflects the *current* losing streak, not the total number of losses in the lookback window.
+
+By default, this also stops trading bot-wide once `trade_limit` consecutive losses have occurred across all pairs combined - not just for one specific pair - since a losing streak can be a sign that current market conditions don't suit the strategy in general. Set `only_per_pair` to `true` to disable this bot-wide check and only ever lock the individual pair that produced the losing streak.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair (and the bot as a whole) for 2 hours after 4 losing trades occurred in a row within the last 2 days.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 48,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 8,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
